Guard the curl header include the way its call site already is.

NetSurf's build has a NETSURF_USE_CURL switch, and content/fetchers/Makefile
honours it by dropping curl.c from the source list. content/fetch.c honours it
too -- the fetch_curl_register() call is inside `#ifdef WITH_CURL`. The
`#include` three hundred lines above it is not, so a build with the switch OFF
stops at a missing curl/curl.h having never needed anything from it.

This port turns curl off because the OS has its own TLS and TCP stack and its
own HTTPS client (docs/TLS.md), so libcurl and openssl would be two large
dependencies ported for something already written. One line, and it is the
only patch the port carries.

--- a/netsurf/content/fetch.c
+++ b/netsurf/content/fetch.c
@@ -54,7 +54,9 @@
 #include "content/fetchers.h"
 #include "content/fetchers/resource.h"
 #include "content/fetchers/about/about.h"
+#ifdef WITH_CURL
 #include "content/fetchers/curl.h"
+#endif
 #include "content/fetchers/data.h"
 #include "content/fetchers/file/file.h"
 #include "javascript/fetcher.h"
